      <section>
      <title>Senior Contributing Authors:</title>
      <list bullet-style="none">
        <item>Lynn Marecek, Santa Ana College </item>
        <item>MaryAnne Anthony-Smith, Formerly of Santa Ana College </item>
        <item>Andrea Honeycutt Mathis, Northeast Mississippi Community College </item>
        <item>Jay Abramson, Arizona State University </item>
        <item>Sharon North, St. Louis Community College </item>
        <item>Amy Baldwin, University of Central Arkansas </item>
      </list>
      </section>
      <para>Algebra 1 was authored by OpenStax and is based, in part, on the OpenStax Prealgebra, Elementary Algebra, Intermediate Algebra, and College Algebra materials, and the IM 6–12 Math™ by Illustrative Mathematics®. Based on OpenStax’s open (CC-BY) license, educators may remix and reuse the elements and content in Algebra 1 according to their approach. OpenStax textbooks are always free online.</para>
      <para>All OpenStax textbooks undergo a rigorous review process. However, like any professional-grade textbook, errors sometimes occur. If you have a correction to suggest, submit it to k12@openstax.org. We review your suggestions and make the necessary changes. </para>
      <figure>
        <media alt="Insert Alt Text">
          <image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/Algebra-1_00_01_01_08.png" />
        </media>
      </figure>
      <para>Students who don’t complete Algebra 1 have just a 1 in 5 chance of graduating from high school. Increasing access to rigorous, engaging, standards-aligned Algebra content helps prepare more students to succeed in higher-level mathematics. </para>
      <list>
        <item>Algebra 1 is a critical “gateway course” in K12 education. </item>
        <item>Success in Algebra 1 is a predictor of on-time graduation rates, success in higher-level mathematics, and post-secondary success. </item>
        <item>OpenStax Algebra 1 is a High-Quality Instructional Material designed for secondary Algebra instruction. </item>
      </list>
      <para>OpenStax Algebra 1 is a complete Algebra 1 curriculum and an open education resource (OER) that is standards-aligned, easy to implement, supportive of diverse learners, and engaging for students. Algebra 1 is supported by instructional support resources, including implementation guidance, pacing suggestions, and ancillary engagement materials. </para>
      <para>ISBN: 978-1-961584-47-1<newline />
            E-book, digital online<newline />
            Publication date: February 1, 2023</para>
